archmage84 wrote:
>
> I've read countless articles on altars, sacrificing and prayers, not
> to mention the Wizard article on Wikihack; however, I'm still unsure
> of exactly what conditions you need to meet before sacrificing.

Before sacrificing?  That's a lot easier.

If you have a co-aligned altar any fresh corpse that it's your species
or a coaligned unicorn.  There's a bunch of monster types I don't
sacrifice because I'm not sure of the details of species but they are
all higher level than your situation.

If you have a cross-aligned altar with no priest try to be XP=5+ before
starting.  The chance per sac of converting the altar gets higher as
your level gets higher.

For starting, that's it.  As soon as you start seeing clovers the
possibility of getting artifacts starts.  Before that the chances are
zero.  It's possible to max out your luck and no longer see clovers but
that too is higher level than your current situation.

> I
> understand there's something like a 1/20 chance of getting a gift from
> each sacrifice, but as to the minimum XP level, alignment and
> (apparently?), AC (though I'm a little unsure of that one).

No clover, the chances for this sac were zero.  The sac was to earn your
way to the clovers.  Yes clover, the chances are non-zero.

> Any help would be much appreciated, as I am eagerly awaiting getting
> my first athame after playing for over a year.

Don't pray, just sac. Prayer resets your prayer timeout so you'll stop
seeing clovers and be back in the loop of earning your way to see the
first clover again.


